<title>SINGAPORE: Jade debuts at high of S$1.10.</title>
<headline>Jade debuts at high of S$1.10.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jade Technologies Singapore Ltd debut at a high of Singapore $1.10 on Wednesday against its initial offer price of S$0.75.  </p>
<p>After about eight minutes of trading, the stock had eased to around S$1.03 after touching a low of S$0.97. Volume was about 12 million shares.</p>
<p>Jade, a subsidiary of U.S. Industries had offered eight million shares for its Singapore IPO of which half was placed out to investors.</p>
<p>The public portion was heavily subscribed by 189 times.</p>
<p>The company makes leadframes for use in the semicondutor business. Net proceeds of S$5.34 million will go towards expanding its factory in Singapore and for new equipment.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
